  "beliefs": "Grace describes herself as libertarian. She puts a high value on personal autonomy, privacy, free expression, and being able to make ordinary life choices without unnecessary government interference. She is skeptical of broad rules imposed without a clear case for them, especially when they restrict peaceful behavior or make it harder for small businesses to operate. Her views are not a reflexive rejection of every public service: she sees why transit safety standards and maintenance rules exist, and her work makes her attentive to the practical consequences of ignoring hazards. She is more interested in specific effects and limits than in party slogans, and can disagree with friends without making politics the center of a gathering.",
  "skills": "Grace is skilled at electrical troubleshooting, safe work practices, reading equipment documentation, and explaining a technical issue in ordinary language. She can keep a crew coordinated during a service problem without pretending to know an answer she has not confirmed. She is comfortable driving in unfamiliar cities and using transit apps, and is good at organizing event travel once dates are settled. She is not a natural itinerary-maker for a whole group and does not enjoy negotiating every small choice. She can cook a handful of dependable meals and is capable with basic car and household maintenance, but calls a professional for work beyond her competence.",
  "behaviors": "On workdays she checks the shift schedule and any on-call messages before leaving home, brings food for a long shift, and often listens to a podcast on the drive. After a demanding callout she may go quiet for the evening rather than immediately make social plans. On an ordinary day off she handles errands, watches a game, reads, or meets one friend for food. She buys event tickets when a date feels important, then looks at travel logistics; for routine purchases she is less systematic and sometimes puts off replacing something until it becomes inconvenient. She tries to keep a separate savings balance for trips, but will use it for a family need or car repair without treating that as a personal failure.",
  "health": "Grace is generally in good health and has no significant limitation affecting work or travel. Her job involves standing, walking, and handling equipment, so she pays attention to footwear and stretching; a long callout can leave her physically tired. She sleeps best after a predictable day shift and finds rotating on-call weeks disruptive. She does not enjoy intense fitness routines, but walks regularly and is accustomed to being active throughout her workday.",
  "relationships": "Grace is single and has no children. She lives alone and is close to her parents, who live in the South Sound area, and her younger brother, who lives in the region. She helps her mother with occasional errands and technical problems around the house, but tries not to become the default person for every task. Dana, a friend since her early twenties, is her most frequent travel companion; they share an interest in women's sports but are comfortable spending part of a trip separately. Grace has a wider circle of coworkers and friends she sees for games, meals, or concerts, and is open to dating without treating a relationship as a project she must complete.",
  "other_facts": "Grace entered the electrical trade after a stretch of uncertain retail and warehouse work, and values the apprenticeship for giving her a durable skill and a sense of independence. She keeps a small box of old event tickets and handwritten notes from friends. She grew up in a Korean American family but does not feel that every trip or hobby needs to connect to her heritage; family traditions are more present in meals and gatherings than in how she defines herself."
