  "education": "She earned a bachelor's degree in studio art, concentrating on printmaking. She liked working with materials and processes more than the prospect of making a living from selling her own art. After college, she took an entry-level job in a framing shop and learned conservation framing on the job. Later, she took small-business bookkeeping and management classes through local programs. She has no graduate degree and does not regret choosing hands-on training over more school.",
  "long_term_goals": "Grace wants her framing business to remain healthy without expanding into a larger, more demanding operation. She is gradually training a senior employee to handle routine decisions so she can be away for longer stretches without feeling that every order depends on her. Personally, she hopes to take a two- or three-week materials-focused course abroad within the next few years, but only when the shop can manage without her. Paying down her mortgage and maintaining a retirement cushion matter too; she does not treat either goal as a reason to postpone every enjoyable thing until later.",
  "occupation": {
    "role": "Owner of a small custom framing and conservation-framing shop.",
