  "beliefs": "Grace identifies as libertarian. She places a high value on individual choice, privacy, and freedom of expression, and is skeptical of government restrictions on both personal life and ordinary business activity. Her experience running a shop makes her particularly impatient with complicated rules that seem disconnected from actual risks. That does not mean she sees every regulation as pointless: she supports clear safety requirements and accepts that people can cause harm to others. She is not a political activist and does not assume that people who disagree with her are acting in bad faith.",
  "skills": "She has strong practical knowledge of framing materials, paper, mounting methods, and how to handle delicate artwork safely. She is capable at pricing jobs, training employees, and explaining technical options in language customers understand. She can manage the shop's finances but does not enjoy tax and insurance paperwork. She is a competent driver and independent traveler, though she is not especially interested in navigating difficult backcountry routes or learning every local transit system in advance.",
  "behaviors": "She opens the shop early on weekdays and usually checks the day’s custom orders before speaking with customers. At home she tends to cook a simple dinner, read, or make a quick list of errands for the next day; those lists are not always completed in order. Before traveling, she reviews outstanding work with her senior employee and tries to finish delicate jobs herself. She saves toward travel in a separate account, but has occasionally decided to pay for a class before she has settled every other financial priority. When she has a free day, she prefers one appealing plan and room to change her mind.",
  "health": "Grace is generally well and stays active through walking and the physical parts of her work. Repetitive cutting and handling can leave her hands or shoulders stiff after a busy stretch, so she takes breaks when she remembers and changes tasks rather than pushing through every ache. She has no known condition that regularly limits her travel or daily activities.",
  "relationships": "Grace is single and has no children. She lives alone and is not currently dating anyone seriously. Her mother lives in the wider Eugene area and is independent; Grace helps with occasional errands or a practical problem but is not her full-time caregiver. She has a younger brother in California whom she calls regularly, though they see each other only a few times a year. Her close friends are mostly people she has known since school or through the arts community. She values family connection, but does not regard marriage or parenthood as prerequisites for a complete life.",
  "other_facts": "Grace moved to Eugene in her early twenties for a short arts-related job and stayed after finding both a working community and a place where she could afford to build a small business. Buying the shop instead of trying to establish herself as a full-time studio artist was a deliberate choice: she wanted a creative life with reliable work and direct contact with the people using it."
