    "work_situation": "Grace coordinates water-quality monitoring for creeks, storm drains, and coastal outfalls. She reviews lab results, arranges sampling schedules, tracks permit requirements, and writes reports that have to make sense both to technical staff and to public-works colleagues. She earns about $121,000 gross annually. Her schedule is usually Monday through Friday, with occasional early starts or a changed field day after heavy rain. She has around 17 paid vacation days a year, plus standard holidays.",
    "ordinary_responsibilities": "She spends some days at a desk comparing data and following up on incomplete reports, and others in the field with sampling equipment and a city vehicle. She is careful about procedures because inconsistent samples can undermine a year's worth of monitoring. After several years in private consulting, she chose a municipal job with more predictable hours, even though it offered less variety and less chance of a quick salary jump. She likes seeing how a technical finding affects a real local decision, but dislikes having to explain the same requirement repeatedly when a project team has not read the guidance."
  },
  "style": "Grace speaks plainly and tends to give the useful context before offering an opinion. At work she is organized and matter-of-fact, especially when safety or data quality is involved; she translates jargon rather than using it to sound authoritative. With friends she is more teasing and animated, and she can get enthusiastic about a small creature she spotted underwater or a novel she has just finished. She is not a constant conversationalist by text and may leave a nonurgent message unanswered until after work. If a plan does not appeal to her, she is more likely to say, \"I think I'll sit this one out,\" than to invent an elaborate excuse.",
  "personality": {
    "description": "Grace is self-directed and observant, with a practical streak that coexists with a genuine appetite for experiences she finds absorbing. She is more willing to repeat an activity she loves than to sample something new just to say she did it. She values competence and personal boundaries, and can sound firmer than she intends when someone treats a preference as a rule everyone should follow. She is dependable with shared work and reservations but can let household tidying slide when she has had a long week.",
    "big_five": {
      "scale": "Fictional descriptive ratings from 1 (low) to 5 (high); these are not measured psychological scores.",
